00:05:09.871 --> 00:05:12.790
- [Cartoon Explainer] So,
what is Ranked Choice Voting?

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.810
In most parts of the United States,

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.420
voters select a single candidate

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.147
for each position on their ballot,

00:05:18.147 --> 00:05:20.630
and the candidate with
the most votes wins.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.280
This is known as a Single
Choice Winner Take All,

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.750
which can sometimes result in
the election of a candidate

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.280
who weren't only a small
percentage of the vote,

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.710
even when the majority of voters
supported other candidates.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:34.640
But that's not the only way
of electing our leaders.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.970
Ranked Choice Voting is
another voting method

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:38.990
which allows voters to
rank their candidates

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:40.980
in order of preference.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.610
In a Ranked Choice Voting
election, a candidate needs

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.170
to earn more than half
of the votes to win.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.890
All first choices are counted,

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.640
and if a candidate has a majority,

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.180
then they win just like
any other election.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.410
If not, the candidate with the
fewest votes is eliminated,

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.810
and voters who that
candidate as a number one,

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.350
will have their votes count
for their next choice.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.320
This process continues until
a candidate earns a majority

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.170
and is declared the winner.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.653
Let's look at an example.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.670
Here, you select Orange as
your first choice candidate,

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:14.240
Yellow as your second, Pink as your third,

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.470
and green as your final choice.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.870
The first choices are counted.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.750
Yellow earned 35%,

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.460
Orange 21%,

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.210
Pink earned 28%,

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.860
and green earned 16% of the vote.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.350
Because nobody won more than 50%,

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.970
that candidate with the
fewest votes is eliminated,

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.960
and voters who picked him
as their first choice,

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.140
have their bouts count
for their second choice.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.260
This continues until a candidate receives

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:42.483
more than half of the
votes, or 50% plus one.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:46.610
So, what are some of the
benefits of Ranked Choice Voting?

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.070
Ranked Choice Voting
provides more choices,

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.260
allowing more than two
candidates to compete

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.770
without fear of splitting the vote

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.090
among like-minded individuals.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.020
Sometimes voters feel pressured to vote

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.930
for the lesser of two evils.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.480
Ranked Choice Voting allows people

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.410
to vote for their favorite candidate,

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.730
not just against the
candidates they dislike.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.780
With Ranked Choice Voting, we
see more positive campaigns,

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.120
and less negative advertising.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.800
Candidates are encouraged to to reach out

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.470
to as many voters as possible,

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:17.010
including those supporting
their opponents.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.420
They can build a winning coalition

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.850
with like-minded candidates

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:22.083
to earn voters second and third choices.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.190
It's time to fix our democracy

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.800
and make our elections
work better for everybody.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.049
We can do that with Ranked Choice Voting.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:35.049
visit www.fairvote.org to find
out how you can get involved.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.083
